    <l n="5" type="heading" level="2" para="true">VIII. Id quod ex femine producitur</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="2">est aliquod vivum cum generante ejusdem</l>
    <l n="7" type="heading" level="2">speciei, sape etiam in alius adjunctis ipsi</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="2">simile.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">§. Qua ratione similitudo respectu</l>
    <l n="10">speciei intelligi debeat, jam explicatum</l>
    <l n="11">est. Nunc declarandum: <i>Unde pendeat?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">Responsio vero facilis est: nempe ab</l>
    <l n="13">univocæ causæ similitudine seu conv-</l>
    <l n="14">enientia. At vero <i>unde similitudo respectu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>accidentium proveniat</i>, ulterius est in-</l>
    <l n="16">quirendum? Dico vero: quod eadem illa</l>
    <l n="17">causa fit, attamen non ita necessaria,</l>
    <l n="18">proinde facilior respectu hujus datur</l>
    <l n="19">aberratio, maxime si generatio à di-</l>
    <l n="20">stinctis partialibus principiis procedat.</l>
    <l n="21" type="heading" level="2" para="true">IX. Ex eo femine prima partes con-</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="2">stituuntur ope spiritus infiti ab anima</l>
    <l n="23" type="heading" level="2">quæ femini inexistit: at postea constitutæ</l>
    <l n="24" type="heading" level="2">partes debito alimento augentur.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">§. 1. Arist. 1. 4. de gen. anim. c. 1.</l>
    <l n="26">docet femen habere rationem efficien-</l>
    <l n="27">tis, at sanguinem menstruum rationem</l>
    <l n="28">materiæ: atque ita efficientis istius in</l>
    <l n="29">materiam influxu partes conformari.</l>
